+# Six scripts share a git helper
+originator: kouko
+kind: engineering
+needs-design: no — internal refactor, no surface the user reads or types into
+status: confirmed 2026-09-02
+
+## Problem
+Six scripts each carry the same Git command-running code, so a single internal behavior has six copies to maintain.
+
+## Proposed outcome
+Extract the duplicated behavior into one shared helper and make all six scripts use it without changing their observable behavior.
+
+## Acceptance
+1. The Git command-running behavior has one implementation shared by all six scripts.
+2. Every script still produces the same output and reports Git failures the same way.
+3. Automated tests detect both behavior regressions and a return of per-script copies.
+
+## Constraints
+- Keep the change internal; do not alter script inputs or outputs.
+- Add no third-party dependency.
+
+## Out of scope
+- Adding new script features or changing Git commands.
+
+## Open questions
+- none

